// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Process Masquerading via Invisible Zero-Width Unicode in Image Path
// Sigma ID: 21825281-f6d7-4996-99ee-39796a282dec
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-10-01 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027.018, T1036
// Description: Detects the execution of a process whose image path contains an invisible zero-width Unicode
//   character (U+200B, U+200C, U+200D, U+2060 or U+FEFF). Adversaries insert such characters into
//   file names so that a malicious binary looks identical to a legitimate one (e.g. "calc.exe") in
//   Explorer, task lists and during manual triage, while evading exact-match path based allow lists
//   and detections.
// False positives:
//   - Executables stored in user folders whose names contain emoji sequences, which use the zero-width joiner (U+200D) to combine emoji
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/388942adbd9641f4dfdcf079d7efe9a75ec0ac43/atomics/T1027.018/T1027.018.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/fb1a1fc96066014224c6550f6447f23689b7661d/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_image_zero_width_unicode.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "​" or FolderPath contains "‌" or FolderPath contains "‍" or FolderPath contains "⁠" or FolderPath contains "﻿"
